devin-search-mcp vendors dsh-devin-search at commit 4fc16d26b24b4df72fc02f3f04e593e832c79d03
(https://github.com/mimimaster/dsh-devin-search), MIT.

The vendored tree keeps its own LICENSE and NOTICE. Protocol field numbers,
role encoding, OAuth endpoint conventions, and the completion message design
were adapted by that project from MIT-licensed piwin sources. See
third_party/dsh-devin-search/NOTICE.

Local changes:
- src/code-search.ts accepts an optional turn budget (1 through 6, default 6)
  and records literal rg patterns on the success result as keywords. Each turn
  runs up to eight commands. The first model message is a depth-limited
  repository map (default 3, at most about 250KB) instead of only a root
  listing. tree_depth, exclude_paths, and max_results (1 through 8) are
  optional. Answer ranges are still re-read locally.
- src/protocol.ts repairs a trailing comma or an unquoted key in one complete
  tool-call object. Truncated JSON still fails. Stream trailers are unchanged.
- src/local.ts runs literal rg through the bundled ripgrep binary with
  --fixed-strings. A missing binary falls back to the bounded JavaScript
  scan. Secrets, symlinks, and gitignore skips are still applied to hits.
- Before the model runs, a smart-case literal probe of the query tokens adds
  matching paths and up to four hotspot directories to the map. This follows
  the fast-context-mcp 1.5.2 hotspot map, without its extra bootstrap model
  round, BM25 file-header scan, git history score, or regex ripgrep.
- If the model never returns a parseable answer, the same search retries at
  most two likely subdirectories inside the original deadline. A verified
  empty answer is not retried.
- After a search, remaining result slots are filled from the literal patterns
  the model already ran. Those files are re-read locally and labeled as grep
  expansion. Lockfiles, images, and README/package manifests are skipped.
- src/local.ts treats a gitignore rule's parent path (`..`) as outside that
  rule. The ignore package throws on `../`. File reads use `O_NOFOLLOW` when
  the platform defines it, and a normal read-only open otherwise. Windows
  Node leaves the constant unset.
- src/oauth.ts tells the browser it can close the page, and marks the
  page as UTF-8. The command allowlist and sandbox are unchanged.
- src/web.ts defaults an omitted result limit to 10. The cap remains 10.

This package does not read Windsurf's state.vscdb, Pi's auth.json, or a DSH
credential file. Its session file is ~/.config/devin-search/credentials.json.
